# Code Style

## Naming

| Area | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Go packages | Bounded context | `domain/wod`, `application/gym` |
| Go types | PascalCase; typed IDs | `WODID`, `StageKind` |
| Go errors | `Err*` sentinels | `ErrInvalidName`, `ErrForbidden` |
| Go files | Role-based | `aggregate.go`, `service.go`, `*_handler.go` |
| TS/Vue files | camelCase modules, PascalCase components | `wodSchemas.ts`, `StageEditor.vue` |
| CSS classes | BEM-like | `.stage-editor__header`, `.alert--error` |

## Error Handling

**Backend:** Domain/app sentinel errors propagate unchanged. Wrap only at IO boundaries: `fmt.Errorf("save wod: %w", err)`. Map to HTTP in `delivery/http` via `errors.Is` — never leak internals on 500.

**Frontend:** Return `Result<T>` from API/composables; check `.ok` before using `.value`.

## Imports

- Go: alias by layer (`appwod`, `domainwod`, `appauthz`)
- TS: `@/` path alias; use `import type` for type-only imports

## Documentation

Code should be self-explanatory. Add comments only for non-obvious domain rules. Update `docs/` when changing extensibility contracts.
